## D. Workflow Designer — write endpoints are entirely missing · CR-14 · P0

**Where:** workflow authoring.
**Current (re-confirmed 2026-06-24):** the API exposes only **reads + lifecycle** for workflows. Present: `GET /workflows`, `GET /workflows/{id}`, `GET /workflows/{id}/versions`, `GET /workflow-versions/{id}` (+ `clone`, `validate`, `publish`, `archive`), `GET .../stages|transitions|fields|field-groups|graph`, `GET /workflow-actions`, and `PUT /stages/{id}/permissions` + `PUT /stages/{id}/field-rules`.

**Missing entirely** (no create/update/delete):

| Resource | Needed endpoints |
|---|---|
| Definitions | `POST /workflows`, `PATCH /workflows/{id}` |
| Versions | `POST /workflows/{id}/versions`, `PATCH /workflow-versions/{id}` |
| Stages | `POST /workflow-versions/{id}/stages`, `PATCH /stages/{id}`, `DELETE /stages/{id}` |
| Actions | `POST /workflow-actions`, `PATCH /workflow-actions/{id}`, activate/deactivate |
| Transitions | `POST /workflow-versions/{id}/transitions`, `PATCH /transitions/{id}`, `DELETE /transitions/{id}` |
| Fields | `POST /workflow-versions/{id}/fields`, `PATCH /fields/{id}`, `DELETE /fields/{id}` |
| Field groups | `POST /workflow-versions/{id}/field-groups`, `PATCH /field-groups/{id}`, `DELETE /field-groups/{id}` |

**Contract rules to enforce:** edits allowed on `DRAFT` versions only; `code`/`key` unique within a version and immutable after use; cannot delete a component referenced by a transition/request; system/default components protected.

**Why:** without these, a workflow cannot be authored or edited through the API — the entire Workflow Designer screen stays on mock/localStorage. Reads + the process graph are fine, so we can already bind the **read‑only** view of a published workflow.

**Acceptance:** create a full DRAFT version (stages + actions + transitions + fields) via the API, then `validate`, then `publish` end‑to‑end, with edits rejected after publish.

---

## E. Seed & enablement

### CR-15 · Seed at least one PUBLISHED workflow version · P1
**Where:** workflow + requests.
**Current:** `POST /requests` requires a `workflow_version_id` that is published. Because authoring endpoints don’t exist yet (CR-14), there is no way to create one through the API.
**Expected:** seed one complete `PUBLISHED` workflow version (stages + transitions + fields + stage permissions) in the live environment, so the Requests screen (the largest screen in the product) can be built and tested before CR-14 lands.
**Acceptance:** `GET /workflows` returns a definition with a published version, and `POST /requests` against it succeeds.

### CR-16 · Permissions seeding for non‑admin roles · P1
**Where:** authorization.
**Current:** after the manual grant, the **platform admin** now has full capabilities (✅ data reads work). Other seeded roles still need their default screen/stage permissions so non‑admin accounts (bank intake, reviewer, committee, etc.) can be tested.
**Expected:** seed the default permission matrix per role (or expose an admin UI path) so each seeded account has a realistic permission set. See the shared seeder for the role list: `docs/backend-handoff/seed/DemoDataSeeder.php`.

---

### CR-17 · Enrich the `GET /requests` list row · P1
**Where:** `GET /api/v1/requests`.
**Current (live):** the list row is a lean summary and omits the fields the Requests screen needs. Example:
```json
{ "id":1, "reference_number":null, "bank_id":1, "bank_name":"...", "status":"ACTIVE",
  "currency":"USD", "amount":120000, "invoice_number":"INV-2026-10000",
  "import_type":null, "supplier_name":null, "created_at":"..." }
```
It has **no `workflow_version_id`, no current stage (`current_stage_id`/`current_stage.name`), and no merchant/applicant** — and `reference_number` came back `null` for seeded requests.
**Expected:** add to each list row: `workflow_version_id`, `current_stage: { id, name }`, and `merchant: { id, name }` (the applicant); and populate `reference_number`.
**Why:** the requests list shows the **current stage** column + stage **filter** + **progress** (all need the stage) and the **applicant** column (needs the merchant). Right now those render empty in API mode. The fix unblocks the full requests list and the request detail.

## Summary

| ID | Title | Priority | Blocks |
|---|---|---|---|
| CR-01 | Consistent success envelope | P0 | all integration |
| CR-02 | Error envelope: `code` + `request_id` | P0 | 409/422 UX everywhere |
| CR-03 | CORS allow frontend origins | P0 | production (dev uses a proxy) |
| CR-06 | `POST /users` role field | P0 | **all user creation** |
| CR-14 | Workflow authoring write endpoints | P0 | Workflow Designer |
| CR-12 | All activate/deactivate/suspend → 406 (+team delete 500) | P0 | status toggle on every screen; merchant suspend |
| CR-04 | OpenAPI accuracy | P1 | typed client, correctness |
| CR-07 | Return `role` in user payload | P1 | user identity/permissions |
| CR-08 | Auth completeness (MFA/refresh/password) | P1 | real sign‑in |
| CR-09 | Document permissions payload | P1 | screen/action gating |
| CR-10 | Banks expose swift/license/status | P1 | banks screen |
| CR-11 | Optimistic locking (`version`) | P1 | safe concurrent edits |
| CR-15 | Seed a published workflow version | P1 | Requests screen |
| CR-16 | Seed non‑admin permissions | P1 | testing non‑admin roles |
| CR-05 | `is_active` default on create | P2 | UX (confirm intent) |
| CR-13 | Document nested write payloads | P2 | merchants/permissions writes |

**Resolved (verified live 2026-06-24):** platform‑admin permissions granted (reads return `200`); **CR-02** error envelope now includes `code` + `request_id`; **CR-07** `/auth/me` (and `/users`) now return `role: {id,code,name}`; **CR-10** banks now expose `license_number`, `swift_code`, `status` (list + detail). The expanded demo seeder is loaded (16 requests, audit logs, notifications, workflow).

**Still open (verified live 2026-06-24):** **CR-06** (the `role` enum is incomplete — see the block above; user creation still blocked for most roles), **CR-12** (`POST /{id}/activate|deactivate|suspend` still 406; we toggle governance via `PATCH is_active` but merchant/user PATCH still reject it), **CR-14** (no workflow authoring write endpoints — spec still 92 paths).

**What the frontend can already run on the live DB today:** reference data, organizations, teams, roles, banks (banks pending CR-10), with merchants, audit, notifications and reports to follow. User management is blocked on **CR-06**; the Workflow Designer and Requests are blocked on **CR-14 / CR-15**.
